With OpenComputers, an Adapter against a P4 machine gives a component. Setters take one call a second (the field's step); a refused call returns nil and the reason.
- bts_quasar: getDisc, getBurst, setFeed, setGas, setField, trim, purge, getLinks, getMilestones, getDirective;
- bts_eye: getEvent, getUnlock, beginTransition, setFeed8, setMode, trim, getSlots;
- bts_mouth and bts_mirror: getLink, getThroat, getUpkeep, setFuel, isOpen;
- bts_junction: getFlow, setRatio, setGain, setOut3, setMode;
- bts_crown, bts_receptor, bts_homogeny, bts_reality, and bts_kerr (getState().link).

[note]Optional: the logic-gate rig needs no computer.[/note]

